  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/interaction.html#dnd\r\n\r\nIn events such as \"dragstart\" the DataTransfer object is available, and in read/write mode, meaning that it should be possible to read the data off of it. However, we don't want to expose file data dragged from the filesystem in that situation, as they have yet to be explicitly dropped on the document yet. \r\n\r\nThe spec should clarify what the correct behavior is in this situation, for example: Include the \"Files\" type in `DataTransfer.types`, include the items in `DataTransfer.items` with the correct `DataTransferItem.kind`, however do not include the file in `DataTransfer.files` and return null from `DataTransferItem.getAsFile()`.",
